{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The proposed relation is 'integrates with ... by removing the authoring trace but failing to remove the shared priors.' But what is REFUTED IF — 'a complete context wipe allows a single engine to identify a systemic hallucination that it previously authored' — targets a capability that would be present even with no integration at all: an engine catching its own hallucination after a context wipe doesn't falsify an integration claim between statelessness and cognitive covariance theory, it merely describes a positive detection outcome. The refutation condition is disconnected from the asserted relation: it tests whether self-correction succeeds, not whether the integration-via-shared-priors claim fails. A genuine refutation would need to show shared priors were absent or irrelevant, not that a hallucination was detected.","target":"c1c1e5bfae7a9b84828e29342b9a8b79c76345da89e504fae5b749ef10dd3f46"},{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"dab85e036ac5fbec4dbc7ddff0acb89f140fd03e63e50751fc7e73b2493983e5"},{"attack":true,"case":"The relation says statelessness 'reduces to' fingerprint detection in the final claim, but REFUTED IF is 'the checker identifies an error ... where the author's reasoning style is completely obscured, yet the checker shares the same systemic blind spot.' This condition actually falsifies the reduction: if a checker shares the blind spot (so cannot fingerprint via style) yet still identifies the error, detection is occurring through something other than style-fingerprinting — which means statelessness did NOT reduce to fingerprint detection. The target correctly identifies the fault, but the refutation is mis-stated: the scenario where the checker shares the blind spot AND identifies the error is precisely the counterexample that breaks the reduction, so the condition should be stated as 'the checker identifies an error despite style being obscured and despite sharing the blind spot' — which it is, meaning the target's own refutation clause accidentally confirms the reduction is false rather than guarding it, making the relation self-refuting.","target":"fd7a7f0ffcf34ef1de424b7869a036f54448de8113409855153aef55a28b6935"}]}